281
00:10:26,822 --> 00:10:29,464
in the Eastern District of Michigan since

282
00:10:29,464 --> 00:10:31,204
December twenty twenty-one.

283
00:10:31,384 --> 00:10:33,343
In March twenty twenty-six,

284
00:10:33,343 --> 00:10:37,261
Judge Laurie Michelson refused the plaintiffs' request

285
00:10:37,261 --> 00:10:39,874
to split it into two separate cases,

286
00:10:39,874 --> 00:10:41,325
one for each system,

287
00:10:41,325 --> 00:10:44,155
according to Pickup Truck and SUV Talk.

288
00:10:44,335 --> 00:10:46,924
So it continues as one case.

289
00:10:47,104 --> 00:10:49,113
No verdict on the merits has been

290
00:10:49,113 --> 00:10:49,600
reached.

291
00:10:49,949 --> 00:10:52,248
So what does a used buyer do?

292
00:10:52,428 --> 00:10:54,251
Listen to a cold start.

293
00:10:54,431 --> 00:10:57,150
A lifter problem often shows up as

294
00:10:57,150 --> 00:10:58,830
ticking or a misfire,

295
00:10:58,830 --> 00:11:01,629
especially when the engine is cold.

296
00:11:01,809 --> 00:11:04,790
Ask whether any lifters or camshaft work

297
00:11:04,790 --> 00:11:05,833
has been done,

298
00:11:05,833 --> 00:11:07,324
and get the invoice.

299
00:11:07,504 --> 00:11:09,830
And if the truck has high mileage

300
00:11:09,830 --> 00:11:11,451
and no service records,

301
00:11:11,451 --> 00:11:13,989
factor the cost of a possible lifter

302
00:11:13,989 --> 00:11:15,399
job into your price.

303
00:11:15,579 --> 00:11:17,543
The five point three is not a

304
00:11:17,543 --> 00:11:18,829
guaranteed failure.

305
00:11:19,009 --> 00:11:20,570
But it is a known risk with

306
00:11:20,570 --> 00:11:21,842
a court case attached.

307
00:11:22,192 --> 00:11:24,735
The lawsuit has had its own twists.

308
00:11:24,915 --> 00:11:27,504
Pickup Truck and SUV Talk reports that

309
00:11:27,504 --> 00:11:30,639
a January twenty twenty-three ruling noted the

310
00:11:30,639 --> 00:11:33,841
claims appeared to describe three separate part

311
00:11:33,841 --> 00:11:37,453
failures, that seventeen claims were temporarily sent

312
00:11:37,453 --> 00:11:40,451
to arbitration, and that some plaintiffs and

313
00:11:40,451 --> 00:11:42,086
attorneys left the case.

314
00:11:42,266 --> 00:11:44,408
GM opposed splitting the case,

315
00:11:44,408 --> 00:11:47,478
arguing it would mean duplicate expert work

316
00:11:47,478 --> 00:11:49,406
and potentially two trials.

317
00:11:49,586 --> 00:11:50,935
Years after it began,

318
00:11:50,935 --> 00:11:53,441
owners are still waiting for an answer.

319
00:11:53,790 --> 00:11:56,183
Engine number four is the Ford six

320
00:11:56,183 --> 00:11:58,857
point seven liter Power Stroke diesel,

321
00:11:58,857 --> 00:12:01,390
the engine in millions of Super Duty

322
00:12:01,390 --> 00:12:01,883
trucks.

323
00:12:02,063 --> 00:12:03,311
It is a powerful,

324
00:12:03,311 --> 00:12:04,559
respected engine.

325
00:12:04,739 --> 00:12:06,867
But one part has become its weak

326
00:12:06,867 --> 00:12:09,461
point, the Bosch C P four high-pressure

327
00:12:09,461 --> 00:12:10,126
fuel pump.

328
00:12:10,306 --> 00:12:12,760
And in October twenty twenty-six,

329
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:15,214
that part became the subject of a

330
00:12:15,214 --> 00:12:18,188
class action that a federal judge partly

331
00:12:18,188 --> 00:12:18,932
certified.

332
00:12:19,281 --> 00:12:22,188
According to Pickup Truck and SUV Talk,

333
00:12:22,188 --> 00:12:24,723
the lawsuit, Droesser versus Ford,

334
00:12:24,723 --> 00:12:27,406
alleges that the pump can send metal

335
00:12:27,406 --> 00:12:29,866
shavings through the fuel system,

336
00:12:29,866 --> 00:12:33,295
which can lead to catastrophic engine failure.

337
00:12:33,475 --> 00:12:36,133
The case centers on lubrication.

338
00:12:36,313 --> 00:12:38,168
The C P four relies on the

339
00:12:38,168 --> 00:12:40,166
fuel itself to lubricate it,

340
00:12:40,166 --> 00:12:44,161
and American ultra-low-sulfur diesel has lower lubricity

341
00:12:44,161 --> 00:12:45,659
than European diesel.

342
00:12:45,839 --> 00:12:49,772
Plaintiffs allege repairs costing nine thousand dollars

343
00:12:49,772 --> 00:12:50,344
or more.

344
00:12:50,694 --> 00:12:54,016
The judge certified classes in five states,

345
00:12:54,016 --> 00:12:56,179
California, Louisiana, Ohio,

346
00:12:56,179 --> 00:12:58,650
Pennsylvania and South Carolina,

347
00:12:58,650 --> 00:13:02,667
covering twenty eleven to twenty twenty-three trucks

348
00:13:02,667 --> 00:13:03,980
with this engine,

349
00:13:03,980 --> 00:13:05,834
according to the report.

350
00:13:06,014 --> 00:13:08,753
The order does not decide whether Ford

351
00:13:08,753 --> 00:13:09,474
is liable.

352
00:13:09,654 --> 00:13:12,695
And Ford argues that some failures came

353
00:13:12,695 --> 00:13:15,502
from owners who did not change dirty

354
00:13:15,502 --> 00:13:18,777
fuel filters, used too much diesel exhaust

355
00:13:18,777 --> 00:13:20,726
fluid, poor-quality fuel,

356
00:13:20,726 --> 00:13:21,740
or additives.

357
00:13:22,089 --> 00:13:23,401
Here is the twist.

358
00:13:23,581 --> 00:13:25,420
There has been a recall on this

359
00:13:25,420 --> 00:13:27,258
pump, but not for the reason in

360
00:13:27,258 --> 00:13:27,970
the lawsuit.

361
00:13:28,150 --> 00:13:30,374
In December twenty twenty-four,

362
00:13:30,374 --> 00:13:33,745
Ford recalled two hundred ninety-five thousand,

363
00:13:33,745 --> 00:13:37,117
four hundred forty-nine twenty twenty to twenty

364
00:13:37,117 --> 00:13:38,695
twenty-two Super Duty,

365
00:13:38,695 --> 00:13:41,349
F-six fifty and F-seven fifty trucks,

366
00:13:41,349 --> 00:13:42,999
according to TFL Truck.

367
00:13:43,179 --> 00:13:46,089
The reason was aged biodiesel deposits that

368
00:13:46,089 --> 00:13:48,389
could build up inside the pump and

369
00:13:48,389 --> 00:13:49,878
cause a loss of power.

370
00:13:50,228 --> 00:13:51,709
And the fix was not a new

371
00:13:51,709 --> 00:13:52,005
pump.

372
00:13:52,185 --> 00:13:53,299
It was software.

373
00:13:53,479 --> 00:13:56,597
Dealers reflashed the engine computer to increase

374
00:13:56,597 --> 00:13:58,123
cooling around the pump.

375
00:13:58,303 --> 00:14:00,836
TFL Truck noted it was unclear whether

376
00:14:00,836 --> 00:14:03,435
this would solve the problem long-term.

377
00:14:03,615 --> 00:14:06,748
And according to Pickup Truck and SUV

378
00:14:06,748 --> 00:14:08,865
Talk, a follow-up recall,

379
00:14:08,865 --> 00:14:11,236
twenty-six V one five eight,

380
00:14:11,236 --> 00:14:13,437
came in twenty twenty-six.

381
00:14:13,617 --> 00:14:15,803
So a used Super Duty diesel may

382
00:14:15,803 --> 00:14:18,835
have had two pump-related software updates,

383
00:14:18,835 --> 00:14:21,233
and still carry the original pump.

384
00:14:21,583 --> 00:14:23,696
If you are shopping for a used

385
00:14:23,696 --> 00:14:24,823
six point seven,

386
00:14:24,823 --> 00:14:26,513
check the recall status,

387
00:14:26,513 --> 00:14:28,978
ask for fuel filter change records,

388
00:14:28,978 --> 00:14:31,302
and ask whether the pump has ever

389
00:14:31,302 --> 00:14:32,288
been replaced.

390
00:14:32,468 --> 00:14:36,210
Diesel owners talk about aftermarket protection kits,

391
00:14:36,210 --> 00:14:38,258
but those are not part of any

392
00:14:38,258 --> 00:14:40,588
recall, so treat them as your own

393
00:14:40,588 --> 00:14:41,082
choice.

394
00:14:41,262 --> 00:14:44,280
A diesel with clean records and documented

395
00:14:44,280 --> 00:14:47,154
filter changes is a very different truck

396
00:14:47,154 --> 00:14:48,519
from one with none.

397
00:14:48,868 --> 00:14:51,463
The recall numbers break down like this,

398
00:14:51,463 --> 00:14:52,955
according to TFL Truck.

399
00:14:53,135 --> 00:14:55,355
One hundred forty-nine thousand,

400
00:14:55,355 --> 00:14:58,338
one hundred eighty twenty twenty Super Duty

401
00:14:58,338 --> 00:14:58,824
trucks.

402
00:14:59,004 --> 00:15:00,718
One hundred twenty thousand,

403
00:15:00,718 --> 00:15:03,718
five hundred ninety-seven from twenty twenty-one.

404
00:15:03,898 --> 00:15:07,763
Sixteen thousand, three hundred sixty-one from twenty

405
00:15:07,763 --> 00:15:08,565
twenty-two.

406
00:15:08,745 --> 00:15:11,834
Plus about nine thousand F-six fifty and

407
00:15:11,834 --> 00:15:13,842
F-seven fifty work trucks.

408
00:15:14,022 --> 00:15:15,848
And in twenty twenty-one,

409
00:15:15,848 --> 00:15:17,164
before the recall,

410
00:15:17,164 --> 00:15:19,502
Ford had blamed fuel that sat in

411
00:15:19,502 --> 00:15:21,986
trucks during the COVID shutdowns.

412
00:15:22,336 --> 00:15:24,317
And there is one more pump recall

413
00:15:24,317 --> 00:15:25,158
worth knowing.

414
00:15:25,338 --> 00:15:26,859
According to Motor1,

415
00:15:26,859 --> 00:15:28,912
in March twenty twenty-six,

416
00:15:28,912 --> 00:15:31,117
Ford recalled seven thousand,

417
00:15:31,117 --> 00:15:34,159
one hundred five twenty twenty to twenty

418
00:15:34,159 --> 00:15:36,364
twenty-two Super Duty trucks,

419
00:15:36,364 --> 00:15:39,482
plus the twenty twenty-two F-seven fifty,

420
00:15:39,482 --> 00:15:42,904
because the high-pressure fuel pump may fail.

421
00:15:43,084 --> 00:15:45,522
A failed pump can stall the engine.

422
00:15:45,702 --> 00:15:48,481
So the high-pressure fuel pump on these

423
00:15:48,481 --> 00:15:50,904
